# How to use this lesson

Lesson 68 ran the charge at |q²|≫m². Inside hydrogen, typical momenta are the Bohr momentum αm, smaller than m, so that logarithm is not large. The finite remainder Π̂(q²) still modifies the photon propagator. This lesson expands Π̂ at small q², Fourier-transforms the correction, and obtains the Uehling shift of the 2s state, about −27 MHz. Expect five to seven hours.

## Learning objectives

- Expand Lesson 62's vacuum polarization at |q²|≪m² to Π̂(q²)≈(α/15π)(q²/m²).

- Convert that expansion into a correction to the Coulomb potential in momentum space and in r-space.

- Evaluate the contact piece on |ψ_{2s}(0)|² and obtain a shift of order −27 MHz, opposite in sign to Bethe's self-energy log.

- Recover Lesson 68's running by evaluating the same Π̂ at |q²|≫m².

